            <div xml:id="d169">

                <pb facs="0258" n="160" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg160"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11048: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-08-03T17:00:00+08:00">August 3, 1930—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 3—11:15 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>661. Legations 649, August 1, 6 p.m. Following from American Consul at Hankow:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>August 3, 3 p.m. Communists still hold Changsha although main body has
                            apparently moved east toward Liuyang.</p>
                        <p>Very strict martial law in Wuhan, all traffic prohibited midnight to
                            dawn.</p>
                        <p>Foreign naval vessels in Hankow: British, one gunboat; French, <pb
                                facs="0259" n="161" xml:id="pg161"/> three gunboats; Japanese, one
                            cruiser, three gunboats; American, one gunboat. Italian gunboat will
                            arrive tomorrow.</p>
                        <p>On July 31st, through <hi rendition="#italic">Monocacy</hi> at Kiukiang,
                            I warned Americans to withdraw from Kuling at once.</p>
                        <p>Jordan,<anchor n="72" xml:id="d169-f1"/> who resigned effective August 3,
                            will remain for a week or 10 days at Nanking.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d169-f1" n="72" xml:id="d169-f1-content">
                <p>Russell B. Jordan, Vice Consul at Hankow.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
